{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791572722,"nonce":"SKH7PSdIfEkm4/NBZQJRVeeNz9g=","message":"Step 5 in part, local in 8fdb2e7bf00b241f1423cb9a91de7dd1660bf798: Div::track(\u0026Interaction) feeds hovered, pressed and focused State\u003cbool\u003e from the element's own pointer and focus events (same transitions as ButtonState), so a bound property can follow them with no Stateful rebuild. Interaction::keyed(key) makes persistent ones. Writes only on change. 7 tests in blinc_layout/tests/interaction.rs; two mutations (always write, leave keeps pressed) fail them.\n\nFound while preparing the toggle migration: bound writes are wiped by a stylesheet state rule on the same node. Filed separately; it has to be settled before toggle, checkbox and radio can bind their colours and keep :hover rules in a stylesheet. The toggle is not migrated yet.","files":null}]}